-- Q1169: Legal Duties and Responsibilities [medium/L3]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Both scenarios require the same ''more likely than not'' standard because disclosure has no effect on the penalty threshold under Section 6694","The undisclosed position must meet a ''substantial authority'' standard (~40%), while the disclosed position need only meet a ''reasonable basis'' standard (~20%)","The disclosed position requires ''substantial authority'' while the undisclosed position requires only ''reasonable basis,'' reversing the transparency incentive","Both scenarios require only a ''realistic possibility of success'' standard (33%) because Section 6694 uses a single uniform threshold for all positions"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Section 6694(a) establishes a two-tier standard based on disclosure. Undisclosed positions must meet the ''substantial authority'' standard (~40% likelihood of being sustained). Disclosed positions (via Form 8275/8275-R) need only meet the lower ''reasonable basis'' standard (~20%), because disclosure gives the IRS notice to evaluate the position on audit.
Wrong (A): The standard explicitly varies with disclosure — undisclosed positions face a higher threshold than disclosed ones.
Wrong (C): This reverses the standards. Disclosure merits a lower threshold, not a higher one, as it demonstrates good faith.
Wrong (D): The ''realistic possibility'' standard was replaced by the current two-tier framework under Section 6694.$EXPL$
