-- Q1174: Legal Duties and Responsibilities [hard/L3]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Both positions meet the applicable standard because ''substantial authority'' (~40%) applies uniformly to all return positions regardless of shelter status","The non-shelter position meets ''substantial authority'' at 45%, but the tax shelter position fails the ''more likely than not'' standard (>50% required)","Tax shelter positions have a lower standard (''reasonable basis'') because shelters involve complex legal issues with inherently lower certainty","Both positions automatically fail because any position with less than 75% likelihood triggers the Section 6694(a) penalty for preparers"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Section 6694(a)(2)(C) imposes the ''more likely than not'' standard (>50% likelihood) for tax shelter positions, versus ''substantial authority'' (~40%) for non-shelter positions. At 45% likelihood, the non-shelter position clears its threshold while the shelter position falls short. Congress enacted the higher standard in response to abusive tax shelter marketing.
Wrong (A): The standards differ based on whether the transaction is a tax shelter — there is no uniform threshold.
Wrong (C): This reverses the relationship. Shelter positions face higher standards, not lower ones.
Wrong (D): No 75% threshold exists in the penalty provisions of Section 6694.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1174;

-- Q1177: Debtor-Creditor Relationships [easy/L1]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Filing a financing statement with the Secretary of State, which is required for perfection","The debtor making the first payment on the secured loan to demonstrate commitment","The creditor obtaining a court judgment against the debtor to enforce repayment","Value given by secured party, debtor rights in collateral, and an authenticated security agreement"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under UCC Section 9-203, attachment requires three elements: (1) the secured party gives value, (2) the debtor has rights in the collateral, and (3) there is an authenticated security agreement describing the collateral. Attachment creates the security interest between the parties.
Wrong (A): Filing a financing statement is required for perfection under Section 9-310, not attachment — these are distinct steps.
Wrong (B): Debtor payment is not a requirement for attachment under Article 9.
Wrong (C): A court judgment relates to enforcement, not the creation of a security interest.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1177;

-- Q1182: Debtor-Creditor Relationships [medium/L3]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The seller has priority because the March 18 filing is within the 20-day PMSI grace period; a March 25 filing would lose super-priority","The seller loses priority regardless of timing because previously filed security interests always defeat later-filed interests","The grace period is 30 days under Section 9-324(a), so both March 18 and March 25 filings would preserve priority","The seller has priority only if the financing statement was filed before delivery, as the 20-day period runs pre-delivery"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): UCC Section 9-324(a) grants a PMSI in goods (other than inventory) super-priority over conflicting security interests if perfected within 20 days of the debtor receiving possession. The March 18 filing (day 17) is within the window. A March 25 filing (day 24) would exceed the grace period, losing super-priority to First National''s earlier-filed interest.
Wrong (B): The PMSI super-priority is a specific exception to the first-to-file rule for purchase money lenders.
Wrong (C): The grace period is 20 days, not 30 days, under Section 9-324(a).
Wrong (D): The 20-day period runs after delivery, not before — it exists because simultaneous filing is commercially impractical.$EXPL$
