-- Q1263: Individual Taxation: Filing/Credits [hard/L3]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Both qualify as dependents because the gross income test does not apply to anyone under age 24 regardless of student status","Neither qualifies because earning $18,000 automatically disqualifies anyone from dependent status under the income tests","Karen qualifies as a qualifying child (no gross income test, student under 24); Alex fails both qualifying child and qualifying relative tests","Karen qualifies as a qualifying relative while Alex qualifies as a qualifying child, reversing which test applies to each"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Sec. 152(c), a qualifying child has no gross income test, and Sec. 152(c)(3)(A)(ii) extends the age limit to 24 for full-time students. Karen meets this at age 20 as a student — her $18,000 earnings are irrelevant. Alex, at 20 and not a student, fails the qualifying child age test (over 19) and also fails the qualifying relative gross income test under Sec. 152(d) because $18,000 exceeds the threshold.
Wrong (A): The gross income test exemption applies only to qualifying children, not to all persons under 24.
Wrong (B): Earnings alone do not disqualify — the qualifying child test has no gross income requirement.
Wrong (D): This reverses the categories. Karen is a qualifying child, not a qualifying relative.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1263;

-- Q1265: Individual Taxation: Filing/Credits [hard/L3]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Both qualify for HOH because supporting any relative in a nursing home satisfies the residency requirement for filing purposes","Neither qualifies because the dependent must physically live in the taxpayer''s home for more than half the year, with no exceptions","David qualifies because a dependent parent need not live with the taxpayer; Ellen does not because the exception excludes aunts","Ellen qualifies but David does not, because the parent exception requires the parent to reside with the taxpayer while others may live separately"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Section 2(b)(1)(B) creates a specific exception for dependent parents — they need not live with the taxpayer if the taxpayer maintains their household (e.g., paying nursing home costs). No similar exception exists for aunts or other qualifying relatives. Ellen''s aunt must physically reside in Ellen''s home for more than half the year.
Wrong (A): The nursing home exception applies only to parents, not to all relatives the taxpayer supports.
Wrong (B): The parent exception explicitly overrides the general residency rule for HOH purposes.
Wrong (D): This reverses the rule entirely — the parent exception benefits David, not Ellen.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1265;

-- Q1266: Tax-Exempt Organizations [easy/L3]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Both activities are equally prohibited and will result in immediate loss of 501(c)(3) exempt status upon discovery","Both activities are permitted without limitation because the First Amendment protects all nonprofit organizational speech","Lobbying is permitted in insubstantial amounts or under the Sec. 501(h) election, but campaign intervention is absolutely prohibited","Campaign intervention is permitted if under 5% of activities, while lobbying is absolutely prohibited regardless of amount"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Section 501(c)(3) draws a sharp line between lobbying and campaign activity. Lobbying (influencing legislation) is permitted if not a substantial part of activities, or under the Section 501(h) expenditure election. Campaign intervention — supporting or opposing any candidate — is absolutely prohibited with no de minimis exception. One instance can trigger loss of exempt status and a 10% excise tax.
Wrong (A): Lobbying is permitted within limits; only campaign intervention is absolutely prohibited.
Wrong (B): The tax code does impose restrictions on exempt organizations despite First Amendment protections.
Wrong (D): This reverses the rules — campaign activity has no safe harbor percentage, while lobbying is the permitted activity.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1266;

-- Q1286: Property Transactions: Basis [medium/L3]
