Wrong (A): The manufacturing origin requirement is a core eligibility condition — not all vehicle interest qualifies.
Wrong (C): This reverses the incentive direction. The deduction encourages domestic, not imported, purchases.
Wrong (D): There is no double deduction mechanism — the deduction applies once to qualifying vehicles only.$EXPL$
