-- Q2383: Circular 230 [medium/L2]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Only if the practitioner has been convicted of a felony related to tax practice","Monetary penalties are not available — only censure, suspension, and disbarment are authorized","Only if the practitioner fails to respond to OPR correspondence within 30 calendar days","When the practitioner engages in sanctionable conduct and a monetary penalty is appropriate given the severity"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Circular 230 Section 10.50, the IRS may impose monetary penalties on practitioners who engage in sanctionable conduct. The penalty amount is determined by the nature and severity of the misconduct and may be imposed in lieu of or in addition to censure, suspension, or disbarment.
Wrong (A): Monetary penalties are not limited to felony convictions — any sanctionable conduct may warrant them.
Wrong (B): Section 10.50 explicitly authorizes monetary penalties as an available sanction alongside censure, suspension, and disbarment.
Wrong (C): Failure to respond to OPR correspondence is one possible violation, but monetary penalties are not limited to that scenario.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 2383;

