-- Q2387: Circular 230 [easy/L2]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Sign the client''s tax returns on their behalf without further authorization","Access the client''s bank records without the client''s additional written consent","Override IRS determinations without pursuing any further appeal or review process","Represent the client before all IRS offices for the specific matters listed on the form"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Circular 230 Section 10.3 and IRS Form 2848, a power of attorney authorizes the designated representative to act on the client''s behalf before the IRS for the specific tax matters, periods, and offices listed on the form. This includes receiving confidential information and advocating the client''s position.
Wrong (A): Form 2848 grants representational authority but does not automatically authorize signing returns unless specifically designated.
Wrong (B): A power of attorney does not grant access to bank records — that requires separate client authorization.
Wrong (C): A representative cannot override IRS determinations; they can only advocate, negotiate, and pursue available appeal rights.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 2387;

-- Q2390: Circular 230 [easy/L2]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Preparing and filing returns, communicating with the IRS, and representing clients in proceedings before the agency","Only representing a client during an in-person audit at an IRS field office","Only providing written tax opinions to clients regarding federal tax matters","Only appearing before the U.S. Tax Court as counsel of record for the taxpayer"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
