-- Q2392: Circular 230 [medium/L2]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Oral advice is not governed by Circular 230 and requires no particular standard of care","The practitioner must not assume the return will escape audit and must base advice on reasonable factual and legal assumptions","Oral advice must be followed up with a formal written opinion within 30 days of the conversation","The practitioner must disclose all oral advice provided to clients to the IRS within the same tax year"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Circular 230 Section 10.37, the standards for written and oral advice are essentially the same. The practitioner must base advice on reasonable factual and legal assumptions, consider all relevant facts, and must not take into account the possibility that the return will not be audited.
Wrong (A): Section 10.37 explicitly governs both written and oral tax advice provided by practitioners.
Wrong (C): There is no requirement to follow up oral advice with a written opinion within any specific timeframe.
